<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner unit wins Hong Kong housing deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner unit wins Hong Kong housing deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Tuesday its 50 percent-owned unit, Gammon Construction Ltd, had won a contract to build a block of apartments in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>The contract was worth 360 million crowns and was awarded by Hong Kong Housing Society, Kvaerner said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
